    {
      "id": "HRV-03",
      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-unit-vector-level",
      "title": "The finite orbit and the level of a unit-vector stabilizer",
      "statement": "For a fixed rational vector of norm +1 or −1, the finite-adelic lattice representatives containing it form one stabilizer–level double coset. The induced integral and principal congruence conditions are exactly those of its orthogonal complement.",
      "hypotheses": "Finite-unramified CM field and self-dual lattice data. There is an initial finite lattice representative containing the vector. K is the full finite stabilizer of the reference lattice.",
